# Depsilo — Cursor Rules

You are working on **Depsilo**, a Go + React dependency proxy cache gateway.

## Architecture
- Backend: Go (Gin + GORM), `cmd/server/main.go` entry, `internal/` for all logic
- Frontend: React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind v4, in `web/src/`
- 12 ecosystem adapters in `internal/adapter/` (pypi, apt, npm, go, cargo, maven, rubygems, composer, nuget, conda, cran, helm)
- UI components use V2 set (ButtonV2, CardV2, etc.) following Stripe design (DESIGN.md)

## Critical Constraints
- **Stream, never buffer** — packages can be 2GB+
- **URL rewrite required** for: PyPI (HTML href), npm (dist.tarball), Cargo (config.json dl), Composer (metadata-url), NuGet (@id)
- **Passthrough only** for: APT, Go, Maven, RubyGems, Conda, CRAN, Helm (GPG/signature integrity)
- **No hardcoded URLs** in frontend — always `window.location.origin`
- **Never ignore Go errors** — handle or propagate
- **All IO needs context.Context**
- **i18n**: update both `web/src/i18n/zh.ts` and `en.ts` together

## Commands
```
make build    # frontend + backend
make dev      # run on :23333
make test     # go test ./...
```

